<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
  <title>Calendar subscription — Prayer Reminder</title>
  <script src="https://cdn.tailwindcss.com"></script>
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Amiri:wght@400;700&family=Noto+Naskh+Arabic:wght@400;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
  <script src="/theme.js"></script>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/style.css" />
</head>
<body class="bg-slate-950 min-h-screen text-slate-100 antialiased" style="background-image: radial-gradient(60rem 60rem at 110% -10%, rgba(16,185,129,0.10), transparent 60%), radial-gradient(50rem 50rem at -10% 10%, rgba(99,102,241,0.10), transparent 55%);">
  <%- include('components/navigation', { user, isAdmin: false }) %>
  <div class="container mx-auto px-4 pt-24 pb-12 max-w-2xl">

    <div class="mb-6">
      <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-1">Prayer times in your calendar</h1>
      <p class="text-slate-400">Subscribe once and the next 7 days of prayers — with a reminder before each one — appear alongside your other events. Times update automatically; this is a live feed, not a one-time export.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="bg-slate-900/60 backdrop-blur border border-slate-800 rounded-2xl p-6 shadow-xl shadow-black/20 mb-6">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-white mb-3">One-click add</h2>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a href="<%= googleUrl %>" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
           class="px-4 py-2.5 bg-emerald-500 hover:bg-emerald-400 text-slate-950 font-semibold rounded-xl transition-colors">
          Add to Google Calendar
        </a>
        <a href="<%= url %>"
           class="px-4 py-2.5 bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-100 font-semibold rounded-xl border border-slate-700 transition-colors">
          Download .ics (Apple / Outlook / other)
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="bg-slate-900/60 backdrop-blur border border-slate-800 rounded-2xl p-6 shadow-xl shadow-black/20 mb-6">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-white mb-1">Or paste the feed URL</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-400 text-sm mb-3">In Google Calendar: Settings → Add calendar → From URL. In Apple/Outlook: subscribe with this address.</p>
      <div class="flex gap-2">
        <input id="feed-url" readonly value="<%= url %>"
               class="flex-1 px-3 py-2 bg-slate-800 border border-slate-700 rounded-xl text-slate-200 text-sm font-mono">
        <button type="button" onclick="navigator.clipboard.writeText(document.getElementById('feed-url').value).then(()=>{this.textContent='Copied ✓';})"
                class="px-4 py-2 bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 border border-slate-700 rounded-xl text-slate-100 text-sm font-semibold transition-colors">
          Copy
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="bg-amber-500/10 border border-amber-500/30 text-amber-200 rounded-2xl p-4 mb-6 text-sm">
      Keep this URL private — anyone with the link can see your prayer schedule (not your email address). If it leaks, change your city in Profile and re-copy a fresh link from this page.
    </div>

    <p class="text-slate-500 text-xs text-center">
      Reminders on this calendar are extra — your email preferences are managed under Notification settings.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-6 text-center">
      <a href="/dashboard" class="text-slate-400 hover:text-emerald-400 transition-colors">&larr; Back to dashboard</a>
    </div>

  </div>
</body>
</html>
